\f0\b\fs34 \cf0 DER DIE DAS TIPS\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 <FOR DER-PLACEHOLDER>
\f1\b0 \
\

\f0\b These endings are male and use the article 'der':
\f1\b0 \
-ling, -ismus, -ich, -ig, -eig, -ent, -ast, -or\
\

\f0\b Examples:
\f1\b0 \
der Fr\'fchling, der Tourismus, der Pfirsich, der Honig, der Teig, der Student, der Palast, der Direktor, \
\
Also, the ending -er mostly uses 'der' (not always). \
\

\f0\b Additionally, the following almost always require 'der'
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b - male person 
\f1\b0 (der Vater, der Mann)\

\f0\b - time: 
\f1\b0 weekdays, months, seasons, time of the day (der Montag, der Juli, der Sommer, der Morgen) \
- 
\f0\b wind, precipitations, celestial directions 
\f1\b0 (der Wind, der Schnee, der Norden) 
\f0\b Exception: 
\f1\b0 die Nacht\
- 
\f0\b car brands 
\f1\b0 (der BMW)\
- 
\f0\b most alcoholic drinks 
\f1\b0 (der Alkohol) 
\f0\b Exception:
\f1\b0  das Bier\
- 
\f0\b most jobs start in the male version
\f1\b0  (der Arzt, der B\'e4cker) - note that some only have a female job title and all can change into female: der Arzt - die \'c4rztin\
- 
\f0\b most stones & gems 
\f1\b0 (der Edelstein, der Diamant)\
- 
\f0\b most animals start in the male version
\f1\b0  (der Hund) and some are die/das (das Pferd, die Kuh) \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 <FOR DIE- PLACEHOLDER>\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 These endings are female and use the article \'82die:\

\f1\b0 -heit, -keit, -ung, -schaft, -in, -tion, -sion, -erei\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Examples:
\f1\b0  die Gesundheit, die Arbeitslosigkeit, die Kleidung, die Freundschaft, die B\'e4ckerei, die Information, die Diskussion, die Lehrerin\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Additionally, the following almost always require \'82die\'91\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b female person 
\f1\b0 (die Frau, die Tante)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b countries & regions that end with -ei, -e, -ie 
\f1\b0 (die T\'fcrkei, die Mongolei) \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b most trees, flowers & fruits 
\f1\b0 (die Tanne, die Orchidee, die Mango) 
\f0\b Exceptions: 
\f1\b0 der Baum, der Apfel\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b cigarettes 
\f1\b0 (die Zigarette, die Marlboro) \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b motorcycle brands 
\f1\b0 (die Harley, die Kawasaki) \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b names of ships 
\f1\b0 (die Aida, die Titanic) \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b numbers
\f1\b0  (die Eins, die Zwei) \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b jobs when explicitly talking about the female version 
\f1\b0 (die \'c4rztin, die Lehrerin, die Polizistin) \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b female version of animals 
\f1\b0 (die Kuh, die L\'f6win)\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \
<FOR DAS-PLACEHOLDER>\
\
These endings are neutral and use the article \'82das:\

\f1\b0 -chen*, -lein, -tum, -um, -ett, -ma, -ment\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Examples: 
\f1\b0 das W\'fcrstchen, das Fr\'e4ulein, das Datum, das Visum, das Bett, das Thema, das Apartment\
\

\f0\b *chen
\f1\b0  only when used as a diminutive (making a noun smaller or cuter) - der Kuchen\
\

\f0\b Additionally, the following almost always require \'82das\'91
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b names of countries,
\f1\b0  
\f0\b cities, islands & continents 
\f1\b0 (das Deutschland, das Peking, das Europa, das Mallorca)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b young animals
\f1\b0  (das Lamm, das Ferkel)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b letters 
\f1\b0 (das A)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b colors 
\f1\b0 (das Blau)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}
\f0\b chemicals & metals
\f1\b0  (das Aluminium, das Uran) 
\f0\b Exceptions:
\f1\b0  der Stahl\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
_____________________________________________________________\
\
\

\f0\b What happens if we put two nouns together?
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Example:
\f1\b0  der Baum + das Haus = das Baumhaus\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}we take the gender of the noun at the end \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \

\f0\b Note:
\f1\b0  Learning all these rules and tips can be challenging, but we hope they will help you learn the gender of German nouns. This can be a difficult task, considering that there are even multiple possibilities for some nouns (das/die/der Band, der/das Moment, etc.). \
\
As a German teacher myself, I am often asked why der/die/das stands for XYZ. The plain and simple answer is: - because that is German.\
\
Mark Twain once said about learning German, "This is what eternity is made for."\
\
